From 9a0d93a6a8258a1c94cafdf3f00486f25a7db3b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:15:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent: float the two thread-navigation controls over the
 conversation

The controls at the end of a turn -- copy this response, scroll to the user
message, scroll to the top -- are rendered by `render_thread_controls` as a row
*inside* a list item. That puts them in the scroll flow, so they leave the
viewport together with the turn they belong to. The two navigation buttons are
therefore out of reach in exactly the situation that makes them worth having: a
long thread, scrolled away from both of its ends.

This moves those two onto the conversation container as an absolutely
positioned overlay, and leaves the copy button where it was.

The split is deliberate, not a compromise. "Scroll to User Message" and "Scroll
to Top" name a destination in the thread and mean the same thing from anywhere
in it -- `scroll_to_user_message_index(None, ..)` already resolves to the most
recent user message, so the floating button needs no index and carries none.
"Copy This Agent Response" names one response, and a control floating over the
whole conversation has no way to say which response it means; mid-generation it
would point at an incomplete one.

Four consequences worth naming, because none is visible in the diff alone:

- The navigation buttons no longer vanish while the agent is generating or
  while a permission request is pending. `render_thread_controls` early-returns
  `Empty` in both cases. That was right for a row carrying a copy button and a
  turn's stats, and wrong for a control whose only job is to move the viewport.

- `scroll_to_top` used to be built only for the bottom-most entry
  (`is_thread_bottom`). Floating it makes it belong to the thread rather than to
  an entry, which is what its label always claimed.

- With both buttons gone, every remaining part of the inline row is optional and
  they can all be absent at once: a last entry that is not an assistant message,
  turn stats off, feedback unavailable. The navigation buttons used to justify
  the row's padding unconditionally. It now returns `Empty` instead of leaving
  an invisible band exactly where they used to be.

- `user_message_index` leaves the signature with its last caller, and so does
  the per-entry `rposition` search that computed it.

The "Scroll to User Message" button is hidden outright when the thread has no
user message, rather than left to `scroll_to_user_message_index`'s second
fallback of scrolling to the end -- a button labelled for one destination that
silently goes to the opposite one is worse than an absent button.

The overlay clears the vertical scrollbar the same container draws (`right_4`)
and keeps the inline row's 0.4/1.0 opacity-on-hover, so it reads as the same
affordance relocated rather than a new one.

Pure Zed: nothing here needs the adapter, so like 0010, 0012 and 0014 it rides
the claude-agent-acp-plus flag BY CHOICE rather than by dependency.
---

